      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to color the hexagons such that no two adjacent hexagons have the same color. We start by identifying the structure of the hexagon and the coloring constraints.\n\nThe hexagon can be divided into three pairs of adjacent hexagons that are in the shape of a cross. Let's label the hexagons as follows:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{ccc}\nH_1 & H_2 & H_3 \\\\\n & H_4 & \\\\\nH_5 & H_6 & H_7 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nwhere \\(H_1, H_2, H_3\\) are at the top row, and \\(H_4, H_5, H_6\\) are at the bottom row. The left-centered hexagon is \\(H_4\\), and the right-centered hexagon is \\(H_6\\).\n\nThe bottom row hexagons \\(H_5, H_6, H_7\\) are directly below each other, and the top row hexagons \\(H_2, H_3, H_4\\) are directly above each other, with \\(H_1\\) and \\(H_7\\) directly to their right, respectively.\n\nTo solve this, we need to ensure that no two adjacent hexagons share the same color. Let's denote the colors by \\(R\\) (red), \\(Y\\) (yellow), and \\(G\\) (green).\n\nFor the top row hexagons \\(H_1, H_2, H_3\\), we have 3 choices for \\(H_1\\), 2 choices for \\(H_2\\) (since it must be different from \\(H_1\\)), and 2 choices for \\(H_3\\) (since it must be different from both \\(H_1\\) and \\(H_2\\)). So, the number of ways to color the top row is:\n\\[\n3 \\times 2 \\times 2 = 12\n\\]\n\nNow, let's consider the bottom row hexagons \\(H_5, H_6, H_7\\). Since \\(H_4\\) is fixed (it is surrounded by \\(H_2, H_3, H_6\\), and \\(H_3\\) is already colored and not adjacent to \\(H_4\\)), we have 2 choices for \\(H_5\\) (it must be different from \\(H_4\\)), and 2 choices for \\(H_6\\) (it must be different from both \\(H_5\\) and \\(H_7\\)). So, the number of ways to color the bottom row is:\n\\[\n2 \\times 2 = 4\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the total number of ways to color the entire hexagon is the product of the number of ways to color the top row and the number of ways to color the bottom row:\n\\[\n12 \\times 4 = 48\n\\]\n\nThus, the number of different ways to color the figure is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{48}\n\\]",
